---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Educational & Legal Disclaimer"
  description="Important regulatory disclosures, educational use notice, and limitations of quantitative financial models under Indian law."
>
  <div class="container container-narrow page-content">
    <div class="badge-row">
      <span class="badge badge-gold">Legal Notice</span>
      <span class="badge badge-blue">Educational Only</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Educational & Legal Disclaimer</h1>

    <div class="callout callout-warning">
      <h3>Not Investment Advice</h3>
      <p>
        InvestiQ RupeeMath is published strictly for quantitative research, financial mathematics education, and conceptual modeling purposes under Indian regulatory norms. 
        <strong>None of the content, formulas, calculator outputs, or scenario simulations constitute investment advice, legal advice, tax consultation, or a financial recommendation to buy, hold, or sell any security, mutual fund, derivative, or insurance product.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Regulatory Status under SEBI Regulations</h2>
    <p>
      InvestiQ RupeeMath is an open educational platform and is not registered as a Research Analyst or Investment Adviser under the <em>SEBI (Investment Advisers) Regulations, 2013</em> or <em>SEBI (Research Analysts) Regulations, 2014</em>. The formulas, XIRR solvers, and inflation modeling tools illustrate mathematical principles and should not be used as the sole basis for actual financial decisions.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Tax Disclaimers under Finance (No. 2) Act, 2024</h2>
    <p>
      Calculations referencing tax rates (such as 12.5% LTCG on equity above ₹1.25 Lakh, 20% STCG, or Section 50AA slab taxation on debt funds) represent general statutory provisions applicable for Financial Year 2024-25 and 2025-26. They do not account for individual taxpayer surcharges, marginal relief, residential status, grandfathering provisions under Section 55(2)(ac), or future retrospective legislative amendments.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Market Risk & Assumption Sensitivity</h2>
    <p>
      Past historical performance of the Nifty 50, Sensex, or any mutual fund category does not guarantee future results. Projections generated by compounding equations assume constant deterministic growth rates, which do not reflect real-world market volatility, black-swan drawdowns, or structural economic shifts.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Professional Consultation Mandate</h2>
    <p>
      Always seek personalized professional advice from a qualified <strong>SEBI-registered Investment Adviser (RIA)</strong> for asset allocation and portfolio structuring, and a <strong>Chartered Accountant (CA)</strong> for personal income tax planning before executing any transactions.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-content {
    padding-top: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }
  .badge-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
